    "description": "The query string is a part of a URL that contains data and parameters to be passed to a web server. It is typically located at the end of a URL and starts with a question mark ``?``, followed by key-value pairs separated by ampersands ``&``. \n\nThe values passed in the query string are available in the ``$_GET`` superglobal array. The keys of this array correspond to the names of the parameters in the query string, and the values are the corresponding values passed.",
